course: dictionary
lesson: 12949
title: Short parts: the excerpt
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An excerpt is a short part taken from a longer book, film, speech or piece of music. When your teacher says «Read the excerpt», she means read the short part she has chosen, not the whole book.
explain: Look for the clues. «Read the excerpt below and answer the questions» tells you the text is short, and the questions are about it. Excerpt is a noun, so you can say an excerpt or two excerpts.
explain: Excerpt can also be a verb in formal writing. «The editor will excerpt two lines from the speech» means she will take out those two lines to show or use them.
fact: An excerpt is a short part of something longer.
fact: «Mia played a short excerpt of her favourite song.» She played only a small part of the song.
fact: Excerpts often come from books, films, speeches and music.
fact: As a verb, excerpt (formal) means to take out a short part to show or use it.
fact: Phrases to know: an excerpt from, a short excerpt, read the excerpt.
exercise: «The teacher read us an excerpt from a book about dragons.» What is an excerpt? | A kind of dragon | A long book with no end | A picture of a dragon | *A short part taken from a longer book
exercise: «Read the excerpt below and answer the questions.» What should you do? | Read the whole library | Read it once, then close the book forever | *Read the short part and answer the questions | Skip the reading and draw a picture
exercise: «Mia played a short excerpt of her favourite song.» Which part did Mia play? | *A small part of the song | The singer's name | The whole song from start to finish | The song's title only
test: «The editor will excerpt two lines from the speech to show the class.» What does excerpt mean here? | To make the speech longer | To throw the speech away | To sing the speech loudly | *To take out a short part to show or use it
test: Which of these is most likely to be an excerpt? | The whole of a long novel from the first page to the last | A complete piece of music, every note included | *A short clip from a film | An entire year at school
exam: Ella says, «Read the excerpt from the book.» What does she want you to read? | A list of the book's authors | A picture on the book's cover | *A short part taken from the book | The whole book from start to finish
